.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payouts-destinations-confirm - Attest the venue credited the proof: the destination becomes verified


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payouts destinations confirm  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Record that the venue CREDITED the proof transfer to your account there. The
destination becomes "verified" and accepts payouts of any amount.

.PP
Confirm only after you see the deposit at the venue — a transfer mined on-chain is
not the same as a deposit credited: a wrong network, a missing memo or an amount
below the venue's minimum can all be mined and never credited. The proof must be
confirmed on-chain first (422 payout_destination_proof_missing otherwise:
\&'rail0 payouts list --destination  --purpose proof' shows it).

.PP
You are asked to confirm (y/N); pass --yes to skip the prompt in a script.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for confirm

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip the confirmation prompt (required to run non-interactively)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payouts destinations confirm <destination_id>
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payouts-destinations(1)\fP
